# Bishon V2 release manifest.
#
# Each non-comment, non-blank line is a path (relative to repo root) that
# ships in the release tarball under `bishon/`. Directories are included
# recursively. Common build artifacts (__pycache__, node_modules, .git,
# .pytest_cache, front_end/dist, bishon_kernel/bishon_server/dist, etc.)
# are filtered by rsync excludes in make-release.sh regardless of manifest
# entries — keep those out here.
#
# To add a ship path: append a line. To remove: delete the line.
# Keep this file readable; group related paths under section comments.

# === Source ===
bishon_kernel
front_end

# === Tests + docs ===
tests
docs
mkdocs.yml

# === Image build ===
docker

# NOTE: `scripts/` and the root wrappers (`start-docker.sh`, `stop-docker.sh`,
# `start-bare-metal.sh`, `stop-bare-metal.sh`, `run_all_tests.sh`, `deploy.sh`)
# are NOT listed here. make-release.sh copies them to the bundle root so the
# bundle is self-deployable (operator runs `bash deploy.sh` from bundle root).
# Listing them here too would create duplicate copies under `bishon/` that
# drift apart from the root-level ones.

